# VTSC PaintPro — Architecture & Development Rules

## 1. System Overview & Technology Stack
- **Backend:** Node.js, Express.js (v4), MongoDB Atlas (Mongoose v8), Socket.io (v4), Ethers.js (v6).
- **Frontend:** Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, Tailwind CSS v4, Zustand v5, Lucide React, Recharts v3.
- **Web3 & Storage:** Solidity Smart Contracts (Sepolia Testnet), IPFS via Pinata Cloud SDK.

---

## 2. Backend Engineering Rules

### 2.1 Database & Query Performance
- **Always use `.lean()` on read-only queries**:
  Avoid overhead of Mongoose document instances when reading documents that will only be serialized to JSON.
- **Index All Filtered and Sorted Keys**:
  Ensure compound indexes exist for fields used in `$match`, `$sort`, and queries (e.g. `createdAt`, `TrangThai`, `KhachHang`, `SanPham`).
- **Eliminate N+1 Aggregations**:
  Never execute database queries inside iterative loops (`for`, `map`, `forEach`). Group data across the whole interval using MongoDB `$group` or `$facet`, then map into in-memory bins.
- **Parallelize Independent Operations**:
  Use `Promise.all([op1, op2, op3])` instead of serial `await` statements for independent collections or KPI counters.
- **In-Memory Caching (`utils/cache.js`)**:
  Cache aggregate reports, KPI summaries, and semi-static catalogs (paint colors, categories) with appropriate TTLs (15–60s) to keep CPU utilization under 10%.

### 2.2 API Response Standards
- All responses must strictly follow the standard JSON contract:
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {},
    "message": "Optional descriptive status"
  }
  ```
- Fast compression is enabled via `compression` middleware with Gzip/Brotli filtering.
- Header `X-Response-Time` is injected into every response to track latency.

---

## 3. Frontend UI/UX Design System Rules

### 3.1 Design Tokens & Theming
- **Color Palette:**
  - Primary Brand: Royal Navy Blue (`#1e40af`, `#2563eb`, `#1A1A40`)
  - Accent / Web3: Indigo Violet (`#6366f1`, `#8b5cf6`)
  - Success / Active: Emerald Green (`#10b981`)
  - Alert / Warning: Amber Orange (`#f59e0b`)
  - Surface Background: Neutral Slate `#F8FAFC`, card surface `#ffffff`
- **Component Styling:**
  - Glassmorphic panels with `glass-panel` and `glass-card` classes.
  - Border radius standard: `rounded-2xl` (16px) for cards, `rounded-xl` (12px) for inputs/buttons, `rounded-lg` for badges.
  - Interactive elements must include smooth hover transitions (`hover:-translate-y-1`, `transition-all duration-200`).
  - Tables must feature sticky header rows, subtle zebra stripes, and responsive wrappers.

### 3.2 Navigation & Layout
- Always render appropriate Lucide icons for every item in `allNavItems`.
- Sidebar must support responsive drawer collapse on mobile/tablet viewports (< 768px).
- Provide breadcrumb tracking and a quick module search.

---

## 4. Web3 & Smart Contract Rules
- Use Ethers v6 standard syntax (`ethers.BrowserProvider`, `contract.getFunction(...)`).
- Always handle user wallet disconnects and chain mismatches gracefully with feedback toasts.
- Document SHA-256 hashes must be verified against IPFS CID and Sepolia on-chain hash before concluding B2B contract signatures.
